<title>JAPAN: Japan Nov tin imports off 18.2 pct year/year.</title>
<headline>Japan Nov tin imports off 18.2 pct year/year.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan imported 1,935 tonnes of refined tin in November, off 18.2 percent from 2,357 tonnes in the same month last year, Finance Ministry data said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The imports (on a customs-cleared basis in tonnes) were as follows:</p>
<p>			Nov 96	   Oct 96	  Nov 95</p>
<p> Total		1,935	    2,357	    2,365</p>
<p>Major suppliers:</p>
<p> Indonesia	  1,019	    1,076	    1,017</p>
<p> Malaysia	     459		461		579</p>
<p>Cumulative imports in the first 11 months of 1996 were 23,222 tonnes, versus 66,054 tonnes in the same period last year.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk +813 3432 7391</p>
</text>
